DeckieChroma is a Swift port of parts of Chromaprint (https://github.com/acoustid/chromaprint), release v1.6.2,
commit 3b38c100022bdfb49be7797c4828a476f1621d55. Only files of Chromaprint's own code, each marked "Distributed
under the MIT license", were ported:

  src/fingerprinter_configuration.cpp   the frame size and step, the chroma filter weights, kClassifiersTest2
  src/fingerprinter.cpp                 the 28 Hz to 3,520 Hz range and the order of the steps
  src/fft.cpp, src/fft_lib_kissfft.cpp  the Hamming-windowed power spectrum per frame
  src/audio/audio_slicer.h              the framing
  src/chroma.cpp                        the 12-note chroma
  src/chroma_filter.cpp                 the five-frame smoothing
  src/chroma_normalizer.h, src/utils.h  the normalising, the window, Gray code, frequency and bin conversions
  src/fingerprint_calculator.cpp        the 32 bits a frame
  src/classifier.h, src/filter.h,
  src/filter_utils.h, src/quantizer.h   the filter shapes and thresholds
  src/utils/rolling_integral_image.h    the integral image
  src/fingerprint_compressor.cpp,
  src/fingerprint_decompressor.cpp,
  src/utils/pack_int3_array.h,
  src/utils/pack_int5_array.h,
  src/utils/base64.h                    the compressed form

Nothing was taken from Chromaprint's LGPL 2.1 parts (src/avresample, taken from FFmpeg, nor FFmpeg's FFT).
DeckieChroma's resampler is Deckie's own; its Fourier transform is DeckieCore's.

